 **Pitfalls:**
-*   **Motion Blur:** ScanNet videos are captured with auto-exposure enabled, leading to motion blur in many frames. This results in poor scene geometries if not filtered [S1].
-*   **Floaters:** In room-centric datasets like ScanNet, fewer images observe the same part of the space. Standard Plenoxels reconstruction may create excessive voxels (floaters) in empty space to minimize image reconstruction loss [S1]. The depth-based initialization mitigates this [S1].
